      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-general-1-2005-p4.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "3\nThe equation simplifies to \\(3 x^{3}+9 x^{2}+15 x+9=x^{3}+9 x^{2}+27 x+27\\), or equivalently, \\(2 x^{3}-12 x-18=2(x-3)\\left(x^{2}+3 x+3\\right)=0\\). The discriminant of \\(x^{2}+3 x+3\\) is \\(-3<0\\), so the only real solution is \\(x=3\\).",
